{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03371",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.34,
      "end_seconds": 3.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Good morning, grab a seat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.42,
      "end_seconds": 9.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "So, hello, thanks for fitting me in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.74,
      "end_seconds": 18.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "Well, good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.64,
      "end_seconds": 22.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "What's been worrying you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.29,
      "end_seconds": 30.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "Um, so... a tight chest at work. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.9,
      "end_seconds": 35.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Right, when was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.49,
      "end_seconds": 44.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.12,
      "text": "For five days, I'd say. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.82,
      "end_seconds": 49.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.11,
      "end_seconds": 66.79,
      "duration_seconds": 15.68,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly. Oh, and wheeze at work. That's been about the same, about four days. And there's a cough that eases on holiday as well, five days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.49,
      "end_seconds": 72.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.21,
      "end_seconds": 77.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Honestly, every other day. It feels mild to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.86,
      "end_seconds": 83.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "So, and what about coughing up blood or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.17,
      "end_seconds": 98.53,
      "duration_seconds": 13.36,
      "text": "No, uh, no coughing up blood, no fever. I did have itchy eyes at work at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.16,
      "end_seconds": 103.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Have you had any ankle swelling or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.74,
      "end_seconds": 109.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "No ankle swelling or weight loss, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.78,
      "end_seconds": 119.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.46,
      "end_seconds": 123.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.06,
      "end_seconds": 127.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.96,
      "end_seconds": 140.91,
      "duration_seconds": 12.95,
      "text": "I've got thin bones. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, um, to be honest. Low haemoglobin, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.36,
      "end_seconds": 144.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Right, and anything else to add?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.39,
      "end_seconds": 151.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "Let me think, I have eczema, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.34,
      "end_seconds": 153.3,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.83,
      "end_seconds": 160.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "Right, I've had an underactive thyroid for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.55,
      "end_seconds": 167.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "Okay, I can see eczema and an underactive thyroid in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.49,
      "end_seconds": 183.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.29,
      "end_seconds": 190.77,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Alendronate, 70 milligrams, maybe, once a week for my bones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.32,
      "end_seconds": 194.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.14,
      "end_seconds": 205.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Iron tablets, once a day. It's hydrocortisone cream, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.32,
      "end_seconds": 216.52,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Actually, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.29,
      "end_seconds": 219.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.8,
      "end_seconds": 231.68,
      "duration_seconds": 10.88,
      "text": "For my thyroid, I believe. My daughter sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.17,
      "end_seconds": 237.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.81,
      "end_seconds": 249.94,
      "duration_seconds": 11.13,
      "text": "Let me think, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.98,
      "end_seconds": 253.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.99,
      "end_seconds": 259.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.95,
      "end_seconds": 276.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.49,
      "end_seconds": 288.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.79,
      "text": "I had a wisdom tooth extraction under sedation five years ago. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 288.84,
      "end_seconds": 298.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.13,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Saturation 99 percent, respiratory rate 18. BP is 118 over 77, temp 36.5 degrees, heart rate 77."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.81,
      "end_seconds": 301.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.34,
      "end_seconds": 307.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.37,
      "end_seconds": 310.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.3,
      "end_seconds": 312.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.13,
      "end_seconds": 333.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "There is a little wheeze at the end of each breath out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.02,
      "end_seconds": 348.01,
      "duration_seconds": 8.99,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like occupational asthma. COPD is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.7,
      "end_seconds": 350.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.77,
      "end_seconds": 387.03,
      "duration_seconds": 34.26,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like occupational asthma. Record peak flows at work and at home for four weeks. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.84,
      "end_seconds": 391.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}